OL,3,ACo-ordinated cattle raids kill at least
OL,4,A72 people in South Sudan
OL,5,
OL,6,FAt least 72 people have been killed
OL,7,Fduring cattle raids in South Sudan's
OL,8,Fnorthern Warrap state, according to the
OL,9,Fregional government.
OL,11,FAn unspecified number of cattle were
OL,12,Ftaken and homes burnt during what was a
OL,13,F"co-ordinated attack" on Monday
OL,14,Finvolving two communities in Tonj North
OL,15,Fcounty, the state authorities said.
OL,17,FSuch deadly violence is often part of a
OL,18,Fcycle of revenge attacks as cattle are
OL,19,Fa main source of wealth and pride for
OL,20,Fmany communities and are also important
OL,21,Fas young men need them as dowries to
OL,22,Fget married.
OL,23,APub: 27-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,320,300,200,140,0,100
